1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,294
The snowball versus avalanche debate is a $215 question.

2
00:00:05,244 --> 00:00:10,230
Not choosing at all costs you $13,600.

3
00:00:10,230 --> 00:00:13,600
Avalanche pays the highest interest first.

4
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:15,692
It wins the math.

5
00:00:15,692 --> 00:00:26,141
On a realistic $10,636 in debt, it finished in 27 months with $2,838 in interest.

6
00:00:26,141 --> 00:00:29,605
Snowball pays the smallest balance first.

7
00:00:29,605 --> 00:00:34,293
It took 28 months and $3,053.

8
00:00:34,293 --> 00:00:37,812
A gap of just $215.

9
00:00:37,812 --> 00:00:40,801
But the calculators miss the point.

10
00:00:40,801 --> 00:00:48,872
A Kellogg study of 6,000 debt settlement clients found the people who actually finished were the ones who closed accounts early.

11
00:00:48,872 --> 00:00:52,744
The snowball closes its first account in month four.

12
00:00:52,744 --> 00:00:56,413
The avalanche closes nothing until month ten.

13
00:00:56,413 --> 00:00:59,239
Small wins keep people going.

14
00:00:59,239 --> 00:01:01,345
So the real answer?

15
00:01:01,345 --> 00:01:04,524
Avalanche, if you trust your discipline.

16
00:01:04,524 --> 00:01:07,758
Snowball, if you've quit a plan before.

17
00:01:07,758 --> 00:01:10,394
Either beats paying minimums.

18
00:01:10,394 --> 00:01:12,730
Follow for the numbers.

